  "_comment": "European midweek + domestic-cup calendar for src/european.py (chip planner). The FPL API has none of this, so it is user-maintained like knowledge_discount.json. `teams` maps a Premier League team (FPL full name, short_name or numeric id) to its competition: ucl | uel | uecl. `matchdays` are the competition's matchday date spans (list every date the round is played on, e.g. Tue/Wed/Thu). A team is 'in a European week' for a GW when a matchday of its competition falls in the GW window (deadline -> next deadline) or within CHIP_PLAN_EURO_WINDOW_BEFORE_DAYS before the deadline. `cup_rounds` are domestic-cup weekends that clash with a PL round; `likely_blank: true` marks the ones that historically wipe most of the gameweek (FA Cup 5th round / QF) so the planner holds Free Hit for them before FPL confirms the blank.",
  "_workflow": "Season checklist: (1) after the previous season ends, fill `teams` with the PL sides that qualified (UCL 4-6, UEL 1-2, UECL 0-1) — an EMPTY `teams` map switches the European signal off entirely; (2) when UEFA publishes the season calendar, verify every matchday span below and the knockout rounds; (3) when the FA Cup / EFL Cup rounds are drawn, set `cup_rounds` dates; (4) delete a team once it is knocked out (its remaining matchdays no longer apply); (5) bump `as_of` on every edit.",
